{"skill":{"slug":"coding","displayName":"Coding"},"version":{"version":"1.0.3","createdAt":1771496638145,"changelog":"Improve discoverability, add homepage and feedback section","changelogSource":"user","license":null,"files":[{"path":"SKILL.md","size":3386,"sha256":"f86d2e8d19f63a8209155190ef03fb1a8a4aa661bb795fdf1e34ec36f4448ace","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"criteria.md","size":1669,"sha256":"875a0396838401740b6632fca5f53b87d811cdee32e57b2a8462553da4fd7256","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"dimensions.md","size":1976,"sha256":"2e7d70b19c99ee7d7f5f376047ffc75c52b1f829103c63facd160e0e21da335a","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"memory-template.md","size":948,"sha256":"796b002981a32ab1b2e2e144e51de8f835b43f0f2f88116e75ecd1bb54f544b2","contentType":"text/markdown"},{"path":"skill-card.md","size":2233,"sha256":"f5744a9d8ed42fb7272218bdd2d69118dccd457e477fb828ab9da39a0a4b6743","contentType":"text/markdown"}],"security":{"status":"suspicious","hasWarnings":true,"checkedAt":1789060973597,"model":null,"hasScanResult":true,"sha256hash":"08b337cb89b850b6c31e05ff7e4165ed7839ce443db29e81c9b43021bd22b793","virustotalUrl":"https://www.virustotal.com/gui/file/08b337cb89b850b6c31e05ff7e4165ed7839ce443db29e81c9b43021bd22b793","scanners":{"vt":{"status":"clean","verdict":"benign","normalizedStatus":"clean","analysis":"Type: OpenClaw Skill\nName: coding\nVersion: 1.0.3\n\nThe skill is designed to store user coding preferences locally within a dedicated `~/coding/` directory. The `SKILL.md` explicitly states strong security and privacy boundaries, including 'This skill NEVER: Makes network requests, Reads files outside `~/coding/`, Modifies its own SKILL.md'. All file operations are confined to its own data directory (`mkdir -p ~/coding`, reading/writing `memory.md` and `history.md`). There is no evidence of data exfiltration, malicious execution, persistence, or prompt injection with harmful intent. The instructions are clear, restrictive, and align with a benign, local data storage purpose.","source":"palm","checkedAt":1779163182854},"skillspector":{"status":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","score":32,"severity":"MEDIUM","recommendation":"CAUTION","issueCount":3,"checkedAt":1789060973597},"llm":{"status":"suspicious","verdict":"suspicious","normalizedStatus":"suspicious","confidence":"high","summary":"This skill is mostly a local coding-preference memory, but one referenced file incorrectly directs agents to update the skill instructions themselves.","dimensions":[{"detail":"Creating and using ~/coding/ is proportionate for a local preference-memory skill, and the skill discloses no network access and no reads outside that directory. The user should still understand that this is persistent local agent memory.","label":"Credentials","name":"environment_proportionality","rating":"note"},{"detail":"The package contains only Markdown skill/reference files, no executable scripts, no declared required binaries, and no dependency or installer behavior in the inspected metadata.","label":"Install Mechanism","name":"install_mechanism","rating":"ok"},{"detail":"SKILL.md requires explicit confirmation before storing preferences and says the skill never modifies its own SKILL.md, but criteria.md contains contradictory guidance about immediate additions and SKILL.md size maintenance. That ambiguity is material because it affects persistent agent behavior.","label":"Instruction Scope","name":"instruction_scope","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"Persistent preference storage is expected, but modifying SKILL.md would be disproportionate and higher impact because it changes future loaded skill instructions rather than only user preference data.","label":"Persistence & Privilege","name":"persistence_privilege","rating":"concern"},{"detail":"The stated purpose is coherent: remember explicit coding preferences locally in ~/coding/memory.md and apply them to future coding responses. However, criteria.md says it is used to decide whether to update SKILL.md, which conflicts with the declared storage target and turns ordinary preferences into possible persistent skill instructions.","label":"Purpose & Capability","name":"purpose_capability","rating":"concern"}],"guidance":"Install only if you are comfortable with a persistent local coding-preference memory, and treat the current package as needing review or correction before use because criteria.md should point only to ~/coding/memory.md and should not instruct updates to SKILL.md.","findings":"[RA1] unexpected: Accepted in part: criteria.md explicitly references updating SKILL.md, which is purpose-mismatched and contradicts SKILL.md's stated no-self-modification rule.\n[EA2] expected: Downgraded: the cited 'without consent' text is a prohibition on observing coding patterns without consent, not evidence of autonomous high-impact action.\n[EA2] expected: Downgraded: the cited 'without confirmation' text appears in a Common Traps warning against storing preferences without confirmation.\n[T02] unexpected: Accepted as a Review concern, not malicious: the artifact-backed issue is an inconsistent persistent storage target, with no evidence of network exfiltration, credential access, executable payloads, destructive commands, or OS-level persistence.","agenticRiskFindings":null,"riskSummary":null,"model":null,"checkedAt":1789060973597}}}}}